11-08 18:24 CST; task 14226\n- **Found via:** queue claim · task 14226 (execution lane: direct, row 5246)\n- **Root cause named:** `verb_claim` claimed via a subquery and re-read the result as the newest claimed row for (queue, worker_id). All lanes share worker_id `repo-worker-code`, so concurrent claims could return another lane's just-claimed task — live repro this shift: lane code-u claims returned task 13384 stamped lane `code-e` and task 8500 stamped lane `code-t`. The caller then works a task it does not own (and the claim guard could quarantine a live foreign claim), which is how a live claim gets displaced mid-work (task 11049 family).\n- **Fix (PR #7882, merged 3674dedfe39c1b6f55cf5b43479953b57ed0b225):** claim picks the candidate id first, claims THAT row with a conditional UPDATE by id that re-checks full pick eligibility (status, attempts cap, not_before) at claim instant, and reads the row back by id. Claim lease and heartbeat defaults are now named constants (`CLAIM_DEFAULT_LEASE_SECONDS=2700` vs `HEARTBEAT_DEFAULT_EXTEND_SECONDS=900`) with `claim_lease_until()` as the single source for the stored `lease_until`.\n- **Tests (oracle: this issue's acceptance):** new `claim_lease_is_the_requested_lease_not_the_heartbeat_default` and `claim_lane_argument_is_stored_verbatim`; `cargo test -p fleet-queue --features queue-broker --lib claim_` → 10 passed; full turso_queue suite 20 passed (laptop). PR checks were QUEUED at merge time (fleet CI stall); merged under standing merge authority on the laptop test verification. Note: the broker binary must be rebuilt/redeployed from main for the fix to go live — merging alone does not restart the running broker.\n- **Links:** task 14226 · issue #7617 · PR #7882 · sibling #7598\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code lane=code-u state=done task=14226 at=2026-11-09T00:47:00Z -->\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/comments/6729